  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under ASC 740-20 intraperiod tax allocation, the tax effect of items reported in OCI is allocated to OCI, not to income tax expense. The $200,000 unrealized gain creates a taxable temporary difference requiring a $50,000 deferred tax liability ($200,000 x 25%) charged directly to OCI.
Wrong (A): While the amount is correct, the DTL is allocated to OCI, not to income tax expense. Intraperiod allocation matches the tax effect to the component that caused it.
Wrong (C): An unrealized gain creates a future taxable amount, requiring a deferred tax liability, not an asset.
