-- Q4903: Income Taxes Advanced [medium/L3]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under ASC 805-740, deferred taxes on identifiable assets acquired in a business combination are recognized at fair value. The $4,000,000 fair value exceeds the $0 tax basis, creating a taxable temporary difference. The DTL equals $4,000,000 x 25% = $1,000,000, which increases goodwill.
Wrong (A): A deferred tax asset would require the tax basis to exceed fair value. Here, fair value exceeds tax basis, creating a liability.
Wrong (B): The initial recognition exception applies to goodwill, not to identifiable intangible assets acquired in a business combination.
Wrong (C): The DTL is based on the temporary difference ($4,000,000) multiplied by the tax rate (25%), not the full fair value.$EXPL$
