Wrong (A): A proportional 15% decline ignores the leveraging effect of fixed costs, which remain constant when sales decline.
Wrong (B): A DOL of 1.65 would imply operating income equals contribution margin divided by 1.65, which does not match the given cost structure.
Wrong (C): A DOL of 2.20 understates the fixed cost leverage. The correct DOL of 3.67 reflects the high ratio of fixed costs to operating income.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 5219;

